# Fleet UI visibility (Milestone 17.2 — locked direction)

## Source of truth

- **Catalog + matrix:** `files/fleet_device_matrix.json` → `capabilityCatalog` slice ([`CameraCapabilityCatalog`](app/src/main/java/dev/pointandshoot/fleet/CameraCapabilityCatalog.kt))
- **Runtime gate:** [`FleetUiVisibilityGate`](app/src/main/java/dev/pointandshoot/fleet/FleetUiVisibilityGate.kt)
- **Evaluation order:** per-camera `featureGates` (when `activeCameraId` set) → catalog `deviceSupported` → live `CapabilityGate` / `HardwareCaps`

## Consumer chrome rules

1. **Unavailable on device** → **hidden** (empty cell / no toggle row). Do **not** show greyed-out unavailable controls on consumer chrome.
2. **Root-only** → stay visible in **`PnsColors.RootAccentBlue`**; tap shows standardized toast via `FleetUiVisibilityGate.showRootOnlyToast` until SU is granted.
3. **7×3 grid geometry** — do **not** remove slots from `previewChromeGridSlots`; render empty `Box` when hidden ([`preview-chrome-ui-lock.mdc`](preview-chrome-ui-lock.mdc)).
4. Log tag **`PNS.FleetVisibility`**: `hidden` (debug) and `rootOnlyTap` (info).

## Engineering hub

Full capability inventory (including probe-only / N/A rows) stays in Engineering / Device Capability Matrix hub — **17.3+**. Do not duplicate catalog rows in consumer Settings without visibility gate.

## Scope

- **17.2:** Eye-AF QS/settings hide; FPS root toast; gate module + JVM tests.
- **17.5:** Full chrome audit (mode dial, format picker, readout, focal row, etc.).

## Do not

- Add LegacySku-only visibility branches without `FleetDevicePolicy` plugin + USB proof.
- Hide features by removing grid slot definitions (breaks locked 7×3 layout).
